  "findings": [
    {
      "detail": "The real Library.resolve returns (base/relative).resolve(); an allowed in-root alias to exact source bytes is canonicalized before original.is_symlink(). The certificate then retains only the canonical target. The linked-source control uses an unresolved fake resolver and does not establish refusal at the real Library boundary. Inspect declared-root path components before resolution; retain generic Library behavior, and exercise exact real resolve/_pin with an in-root alias and regular path.",
      "file": "swdb-project/swdb/dx100_initialized_register_source.py",
      "id": "R1",
      "line": 51,
      "priority": 2,
      "title": "Check logical source path before Library.resolve dereferences it"
    },
    {
      "detail": "unit_policy validates fixed SEMANTICS_ID, but _with_semantics uses separately selected semantics[id] to generate the prelude and record the semantics. source.check does not constrain data.id. A higher-sequence same-layout clone can be selected by proof_semantics.current while the old fixed semantics and its policy remain present. Exact closed-model checks restrict content but do not ensure subject/policy identity equality. Reject selected ID/hash mismatch and wrong source entry identity, with coherent-current-clone controls.",
      "file": "swdb-project/swdb/wp_adapter.py",
      "id": "R2",
      "line": 848,
      "priority": 2,
      "title": "Bind actual selected semantics to the partial policy ID and physical pin"
    }
  ],
